 ## Operating characteristics
-- **Time Complexity:** The calculation involves basic arithmetic operations and square roots, making it $O(1)$ per primitive.
-- **Memory Complexity:** $O(1)$ auxiliary memory.
-- **Performance:** The tight bounding box improves rendering efficiency. On the Mip-NeRF360 dataset, QGS with this tight bounding box (QGS w/ TB) achieved 14.15 FPS compared to 7.92 FPS for standard QGS, with reduced storage (641MB vs 688MB) [S1]. On the TNT dataset, it achieved 25.36 FPS vs 13.27 FPS [S1].
